ActorRoleAssignment is modelled in the EU DPP CO ACTOR module.
Product is modelled in the EU DPP CO P_DPP module."""@en ;
                                            rdfs:label "in context of product"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/eudpp#includesMethod
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#includesMethod> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                        rdfs:domain <https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAMethod> ;
                                        rdfs:range <https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAMethod> ;
                                        rdfs:comment "Link from a Method (a collection of methods sharing a methodology such as \"EF 3.1\") to each of the individual-indicator method instances it aggregates."@en ;
                                        rdfs:label "includes method"@en ;
                                        <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceVocabulary> """ILCD base: Corresponds to the element referenceToIncludedMethods.
ILCD+EPD LCIA Method Data Sets can represent either a single LCIA or inventory method (one indicator) or a methodology (a collection/list of methods); this property is used only in the latter case."""@en .


###  https://w3id.org/eudpp#isActorRoleAssignmentForEvent
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#isActorRoleAssignmentForEvent> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                       rdfs:domain <https://w3id.org/eudpp#ActorRoleAssignment> ;
                                                       rdfs:range <https://w3id.org/eudpp#ESPREvent> ;
                                                       rdfs:comment """Links an actor-role assignment to the event context in which the role assignment applies. This is the inverse of evt:hasActorRoleAssignment and is managed in the Connector/mapping layer.

ESPREvent is modelled in the EU DPP CO EVENT module.
ActorRoleAssignment is modelled in the EU DPP CO ACTOR module."""@en ;
                                                       rdfs:label "is actor role assignment for event"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/eudpp#isComponentOf
