                                                     rdfs:label "Market Surveillance Authority"@en .


###  https://w3id.org/eudpp#massFractionUnit
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#massFractionUnit> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                   <https://si-digital-framework.org/SI#MeasurementUnit> ;
                                          <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> "SI style convention: percent denotes the number 0.01; mass fraction values should be represented as decimal ratios in data."@en ;
                                          <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://physics.nist.gov/cuu/Units/checklist.html> ,
                                                                            <https://si-digital-framework.org/> ;
                                          rdfs:comment "Project-managed measurement-unit convention for dimensionless mass fraction expressed as a decimal ratio of masses. Use dpp:numericalValue \"0.001\"^^xsd:decimal for 0.1 % by mass. This avoids encoding \"w/w\" in the unit symbol and may be replaced by an official SI Digital Framework PID if one becomes available."@en ;
                                          rdfs:isDefinedBy :SOC ;
                                          rdfs:label "mass fraction unit"@en ;
                                          <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceStatus> "Implementation measurement-unit convention; not a named SI Digital Framework unit PID."@en .


