###  https://w3id.org/eudpp#model
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#model> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                        <https://w3id.org/eudpp#ProductIdentifierGranularity> ;
                               rdfs:comment """According to ESPR Art 9 (2d) the digital product passport is to be established at model, batch or item level, and the definition of such levels is given by delegated acts;

The term ‘model’ usually refers to a version of a product of which all units share the same technical characteristics relevant for the ecodesign requirements and the same model identifier (ESPR preamble (33))."""@en ;
                               rdfs:label "model"@en .


